+# Jev conversion plan
+
+Approved: only workflow.py:83, pure DECISION classifier, Choice with confidence gate and original fallback. Conservative; no keys; no push. Output branch jev-convert/demo, original main at 7c497d21099fc916692f1dd45b5a6107b03754d5. Preflight: clean, branch unused, provider none, key_present false; live validation skipped.
+
+Audit: Anthropic SDK / claude-haiku-4-5; simple_classify(X) builds a prompt from runtime text and ten fixed categories, calls client.messages.create at original line 83, strips response.content[0].text and returns a string at line 96. No local consumers, extra wrappers, generation, mixed, or extraction sites. No diagnostics/usage are returned. Prompt is roughly 3 KB plus input; bundled test tickets are at most 352 characters. Public input was unbounded and has no effective injection mitigation. Fit is limited to benign bundled example distribution; no public-service robustness claim.
+
+Options: A (approved), fallback/Choice on this classifier only: accepted decisions likely reduce latency/cost by avoiding generative inference; misses add Jev latency/cost. Expected cost = Jev + fallback fraction * original. Risks: confident misclassification, overlapping categories, uncalibrated threshold, injection. B, leave/none: unchanged site and cost/latency; no migration risk or savings.
+
+Policy: jev_decisions.py owns version jev-1.13.0, original ten label descriptions, instructions, provisional threshold 0.95, 8,000-byte input bound, timeout and gate. Preserve original signature and fallback function body, request, model, parser, and exception propagation. Reject missing key, unsupported state, malformed/low-confidence responses, errors, timeout, or rate limit. No provider selected: default disabled, no network use; future TypeSafe activation requires explicit JEV_PROVIDER=typesafe. No other provider or moving alias.
+
+Validation wiring (before validation script): baseline git source simple_classify loaded with recording Anthropic boundary; production preserved callable workflow._original_simple_classify; public workflow.simple_classify; evaluator jev_decisions.evaluate/parse_answer; gate jev_decisions.confidence_gate; integration jev_decisions.classify. Offline checks import these symbols and compare original AST allowing only rename; capture request and parse behavior. No baseline provider adaptation; original SDK double only. Inject transport exceptions and force rejection at gate boundary with a sentinel (not a fabricated HTTP response). Accepted Jev inference is not mocked or claimed.
+
+Run user-supplied smoke.py with fixture anthropic_classification plus offline contract/fault checks. No live pairs, confidence curve, measured cost/latency or parity claims without keys. Bundled train/test each contain 68 unique labeled texts; future evaluation must separate calibration and confirmation and use the actual original and converted callables. Save plan, audit, skipped parity metadata and final report; run artifact checker and commit approved files only.
